// RSI Mean Reversion
//
// Welles Wilder's relative strength index, traded the way he described: buy exhaustion
// below 30, leave on the return to the middle.
//
// Read its numbers carefully. Mean reversion wins often and loses rarely but LARGELY —
// negative skew — which is exactly the return shape a naive Sharpe flatters. The deflated
// figure exists for strategies like this one.
strategy("RSI Mean Reversion", overlay = false)

r = rsi(close, 14)

plot(r,  title = "RSI",        color = color.accent)
plot(30, title = "Oversold",   color = color.mute, style = style.step)
plot(70, title = "Overbought", color = color.mute, style = style.step)

if crossover(r, 30)
    strategy.entry("reversion", strategy.long)

if crossunder(r, 55)
    strategy.close("reversion")
